  "query_preview": "..\nAs distant Typhoon Dolphin continues west-northwestward, passing \nsouth of Minamitorishima, the developing monsoon surge near the \nMarianas will shift gradually north, maintaining at least scattered \nshowers and isolated thunderstorms in the forecast over the next few \ndays. Shower coverage is expected to focus near and south of Guam \nthrough early next week. Meanwhile, west to southwest winds will \ncontinue to increase, especially for Guam, then spread northward\nacross the CNMI. Moderate to fresh winds with occasional strong \ngusts are expected to become breezy Sunday and Sunday night, then \nwindy, Monday through Tuesday, with near-gale to gale force gusts \npossible, particularly near any heavier showers. A headline was \nincluded to highlight the potential for windy conditions to develop \nearly next week. Breezy west to southwest winds are expected to \ncontinue into the end of the week as TY Dolphin continues its west-\nnorthwest track toward the Ryukyu Islands, with sustained wind \nspeeds hovering around Small Craft Advisory criteria of 22 knots.",
